            "review_title": "Review at Ya! Japanese Dining & Cafe",
            "review_text": "地デジオヤジ\nNara, Japan540 contributions\n0\nA cafeteria serving exquisite tonkatsu with Japanese ingredients\nMay 2025 • Couples\nI went in for lunch cold. A Japanese restaurant serving pork cutlet, fried shrimp and udon. Now, I ordered a fried pork cutlet set. I was surprised at the quality of the food that came out!\nIt's much better than the Japanese tonkatsu chain. And inexpensive.\nWhen I asked, rice was imported from Japan. Pork is from Canada. Breadcrumbs and frying oil are also sourced from Japan. Shrimp is from Nha Trang.\nIt was so delicious I visited twice. Order Ebiten Udon. Udon noodles and udon stock are also imported from Japan. If you're Japanese and you've been to Nha Trang, it's a must-visit.\nThe store manager is a young woman who is fluent in Japanese from Yunan.\nOne regret is that the soup for the set meal is vegetable soup. Please revive the miso soup as it can be a paid option.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nAtmosphere\nTranslated from Japanese\nShow original\nWritten May 19, 2025",
